WEBVTT

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.390
The Unexplored Ruins.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.400
It's surrounded by strong air turbulence,

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.730
as well as floating debris.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.280
Therefore, we can't get anywhere near it with a balloon.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.950
So that's why nobody has reached it yet.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.500
But we will get there!

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.660
We will be the first ones!

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.790
Yes, and that's why...

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.340
We're discussing how to reach it.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.540
I-I guess so.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.170
There's a way.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.010
By airship.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:12.610
By airship, huh?

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.740
It's true that with an airship's propulsion and sturdiness,

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.320
we can overcome the turbulence and debris.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:21.740
Have you seen an airship before, Logy-san?

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:27.210
Yeah, there's only a few people,
but Central City does research on airships.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.830
Then if the survey team from Central rides one here....

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.180
That's not going to happen.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.470
Airships are really valuable.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:38.230
They wouldn't have the resources to assign one to a survey tea-

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.140
Hey, Escha, Logy!

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.390
Over here!

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.640
You aren't at the port?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.590
I didn't know this room existed.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:00.450
The maintenance crew has always dreamed of building an airship.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.840
I also share that dream.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.590
However, since Solle is never willing to give us the budget,

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.460
we can only build it in secret here.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.130
I see...

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.060
Logy, over here.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.210
O-Okay.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.440
This is amazing.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.230
It's nearly done already!

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.800
About 70%, that is.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.520
Finishing her and reaching the Ends of the Earth...

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.730
...has always been my dream.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.500
Ends of the Earth?

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.190
Yeah.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.800
Oh, you were always talking about that when we were kids.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.190
We failed over and over and would make improvements each time.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.870
This is already our third vessel.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.210
You'll make it this time.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:46.950
Yeah.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.620
It won't.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.910
The frame's not strong enough.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.420
As it stands, it cannot withstand the strength of the turbulence.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.960
Next, there's also the fundamental problem of lift.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.910
It's not going to float very well if you try to use hot air as you would with a balloon.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.510
Logy, you...

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.290
The biggest problem is the engine.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.730
Its output isn't high enough.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.220
Exactly.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.160
Chief!

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.060
You sure know your stuff.

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:17.420
This is embarrassing to say, but there's nothing more we can do.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.610
That's why we let it be.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:22.590
The maintenance crew have been trying different ideas, but...

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:27.220
An airship's design cannot rely on mechanical technology alone.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.750
Highly sophisticated integration between it and alchemy is very important.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.100
Alchemy?

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.120
That's right.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.380
Alchemy is used to replicate the technology used in the past.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.630
In that case, Logy-san and I can easily handle that!

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:42.630
It's not that simple.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:47.470
Airships are said to be the cumulation of alchemical technology.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.810
We need very advanced alchemy to build one.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.020
Does that mean...

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.170
...it's not something the two of us can do?

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.310
That's exactly it.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.530
Even so, I think we have to try.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:11.950
If we don't hurry, the survey team from Central will arrive!

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.740
You don't need to obsess over the airship.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:16.990
Let's think of another way.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.970
But it's close to completion!

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.310
Didn't Awin tell us?

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.410
This is the difficult part.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.020
What they need is alchemy!

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:29.850
Logy-san!

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.090
Let's try everything that we can!

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.270
Haven't we come this far because we have been doing that?!

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.440
This is different than what we have done so far.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.470
The development of an airship is very dangerous.

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:45.360
If we make one mistake, it can cause a very serious accident.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.820
Why, hello, the two of you.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:54.290
I heard that the two of you can finally take on those Unexplored Ruins!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.050
Shh! Shh!

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.400
Don't yell it out! It's still a secret!

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.090
News travels fast.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:04.350
Actually, there's something that I'd really love to recommend to you.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.090
It's this.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.760
It's a rather old book.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:10.480
In the ancient language, too.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:12.610
What does it say?

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:17.390
Isn't this a technique for creating gas lighter than air?

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:18.370
Eh?

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.060
Does that mean we can use that on the airship?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.870
We just might be able to!

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:23.710
So what do you think?

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.810
We were looking for just that!

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.130
How much is it?

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.110
That's way too expensive!

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.530
You're just trying to take advantage of us.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.430
Are you sure?

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:37.040
There are other prospective buyers.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.000
Hey!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.790
So, has that book been sold yet?

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:42.440
Harry-san!

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:45.330
Yeah, I am doing so right now.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:46.550
Then... that book...!

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.310
I found it in a ruin a while back.

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:53.930
The contents are intriguing, but I don't have the time to decipher it.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.750
I want this book!

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:57.560
It contains something I really want to know!

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.950
Hm?

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.770
Can you two read the ancient language?

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.220
Yeah, just a bit.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.820
I see.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:09.320
In that case, I'll give it to you.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.250
Heh?!

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.310
Really?

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:12.560
Of course.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:14.990
Just tell me what it's about later.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.360
Here.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.900
Thank you!

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.130
W-Wait!

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.880
And with that, I'm cancelling my commission.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.840
No way!

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:52.200
It's floating!

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.410
We did it...

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:56.740
If we gather a lot of this gas, we can make the airship float!

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:57.790
Yeah.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:01.120
With this, we're another step closer to completing the airship, right?!

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:02.970
By chance, but yes.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:04.710
So what if it was by chance?

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.900
Let's keep at it!

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:08.810
We still have a few assignments left.

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:10.460
Let's finish them one by one!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.340
If everyone works together, we can get them done quickly!

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.430
Logy-san, what should we do next?

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:22.060
Additional ingredients, is it?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.030
Yes.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:25.390
We need the amount listed.

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:28.480
I've heard about the airship from Marion-san.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.850
The branch manager already approved the budget for it earlier.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.650
Please make the arrangements.

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:37.950
Yes... is what I'd like to say,

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:41.940
but there is a severe shortage of the rare metals.

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:46.500
The metal-eating dragon has started to build its nest again, and it has become difficult to gather metals.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.700
Metal-eating dragon?

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.960
It's a huge dragon that specialises in gathering metals.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:56.720
During its nesting cycle, it gathers nearby metals to build a nest.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:09:01.390
Because of that, there is a lack of metals in the entire area.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.200
The metals you requested in particular.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.640
No...

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.630
Will it get any better after the nesting cycle?

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:09.650
After a few months, then yes.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.280
I see.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.860
I guess we can only chalk it up to bad timing.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.420
Is there any way we can get just a little?

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:18.620
Is there any other way to get some?

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.020
I was thinking of alternative means,

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:22.450
but they're all rather difficult.

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.240
I see.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.210
The metal-eating dragon, huh?

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.740
And we were finally seeing the light at the end of the tunnel.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:31.800
It's fine, Escha.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:35.290
Our job is to find a way to reach the Unexplored Ruins.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.430
Let's not worry about the airship for now.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:40.810
I guess the Ends of the Earth are even further away now.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:46.270
Even though Onii-chan said that, he looked very depressed.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.970
The Ends of the Earth, huh?

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:54.130
He told me that he wanted to go to the Ends of the Earth when we were young.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.280
There, the land is said to be covered in green,

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:59.600
the flowers bloom and shine,

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:02.560
and, supposedly, there's also a homunculi paradise!

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.820
He wanted to build an airship in order to test the rumours.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.460
So this is where you are.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:09.790
I've been looking for you, Logy-san.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:10.840
Micie-kun.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:12.960
Do you need something from me?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:16.170
Yeah, there's something I wanted to ask you.

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:23.610
I thought I heard the name Logix Fiscario somewhere before...

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:24.810
I see now.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:32.020
In the past, you helped develop airships and their alchemical engines in Central City, didn't you?

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.680
Yeah.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:34.880
Huh?

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.000
You worked on airships, Logy-san?

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.860
So I take it you also know about the accident, of course?

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.350
Yes.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:44.990
The next generation engine model explosion incident.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.620
You were the lead developer, weren't you?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:48.910
Incident?

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:54.840
The airship prototype was incinerated, and the crew was injured.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.970
Let go! Let me go!

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:14.060
Logy...

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:26.600
That accident became a huge topic in Central City.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:30.790
Logy-san, I probably don't need to tell you,

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.370
but developing airships is very dangerous.

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:37.000
Please stop immediately.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:47.120
At the time, I was commissioned to develop the next generation engine.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:49.020
It's the heart of an airship.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:53.520
I was recognised, and I felt really happy about that.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.150
That's why I worked really hard.

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:58.850
The mechanics thought I was an idiot.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:02.990
They couldn't understand the efficiency of my engine design at all.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:07.530
I couldn't trust those people, and continued my research by myself.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.950
But I made a mistake.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.870
I wouldn't listen to the mechanic's concerns.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:19.510
Simply because how I wouldn't listen, a huge accident happened.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:23.930
Even a friend of mine who always supported me was injured.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:29.710
He managed to survive, but he could never fly again.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.640
I took away his dreams.

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:35.520
I can't face him.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:38.080
The thought of seeing him scares me.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:42.350
That's why I ran here.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:44.050
Logy-san...

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:46.650
I don't have the right.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:53.180
Someone as selfish and uncooperative as me has neither the right to build airships...

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:55.120
...nor the right to fly in the sky.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.880
That's not true!

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:00.350
You're a really amazing person, Logy-san!

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:03.230
You can do a lot of things others can't do,

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:05.470
and you always come to help me!

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.700
Don't say that you don't have the right...!

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:14.070
Even if you failed once, you might just succeed this time!

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:16.150
That's why... that's why...

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.310
You're wrong, Escha.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:19.360
I'm not nearly...

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.190
You can do it!

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:23.700
If it's you, you can do it!

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:24.980
You can!

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:26.460
Escha!

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:33.090
You said you were happy researching airships and that you worked hard!

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:35.910
Isn't that because it was your dream?!

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:37.290
My dream...

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:40.630
That has always been my dream.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.470
Let's build the best airship ever.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:49.350
You can't give up on your dream so easily.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:54.980
It's because you're here that my dream to reach the Unexplored Ruins is about to be realised!

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:58.170
Tell yourself that you can do it, Logy-san!

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.600
If you won't do it...

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:05.230
It's impossible for me to do anything on my own!

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:08.050
Don't say something so miserable with such conviction.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:13.910
I never would have believed that somebody would cry for me, given how worthless I am.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.250
Of course I would!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.210
You're an important friend!

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:19.970
Friend...?

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:23.020
Besides... Besides...!

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:26.300
You are you, Logy-san!

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.800
Okay, let's do it.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:32.010
Logy-san?

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.500
Let's try once more.

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:36.700
That's right.

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:39.140
That's something I can do now.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:42.730
Yo.

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:44.410
Reyfer-san!

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:45.530
Linca-san too!

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:50.040
Swordsgirl and I have a date at the Dragon's Nest later on.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.020
We don't.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:53.310
Dragon? You mean...

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:54.570
...the metal-eating dragon?

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:55.960
That's right.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:59.540
We need those rare metals on the ingredients list.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.290
Isn't that dangerous?

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:04.350
We have an incense that dragons hate.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:06.300
If we use it, we should be able to manage.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:10.160
I want to support everyone too.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.630
This is all I can do to help.

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:13.550
Linca-san...

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.340
It's okay.

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:16.940
I'm going with her.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:19.060
You can leave it to me.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.770
It'll help even if it's just a little.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:25.250
We can let the homunculi replicate them later on.

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:30.820
If this works out, the problem with the frame should be solved.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:34.020
Yeah, that leaves us with this.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:34.780
How is it?

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:37.680
Valve lift mechanism.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:40.410
Design-wise, there's nothing wrong with it.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.240
You really know your stuff.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:43.420
It's my speciality, after all.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:48.570
When I was in Central City, I was in charge of developing alchemical engines.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:49.340
So that's why.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:53.010
However, I haven't succeeded yet.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.570
That's why, no matter what...

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:56.570
Will you let me help?

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.020
Please.

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:04.250
You got it.

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:09.190
The internal combustion engine is the problem.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.530
Internal combustion engine?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.700
To put it simply, it's fire.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.450
And a really strong one, at that.

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:18.150
Fire, huh?

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:21.500
In Central, they used highly combustible liquids as fuel.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:22.580
Oh!

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:25.170
I have a great idea!

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:29.630
I don't really get it, but that sounds like a pain.

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:34.260
So you need really powerful flames to make the airship move?

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:35.470
Yeah.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:38.310
And if it has to do with flame, I thought you might know, Wilbell-san.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:41.490
Well, I do have an idea.

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:42.230
Really?

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:44.730
We need to borrow the power of a spirit.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:45.600
Spirit?

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:54.130
Okay?

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:55.410
Do it according to our plan.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.110
Got it.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:01.230
Let's light this Slumber Incense.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:07.210
With this, the dragon will sleep like a rock.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:16.800
The hell's going on?!

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:20.390
You're kidding me...

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:32.900
I'll never forget you.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.570
Hey, Fire Lord!

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.350
You are here, human.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:43.580
Have you come to make a contract with me?

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:44.550
Yep!

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:48.390
...is what I want to say, but I'm not here for that today.

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:51.590
For my friends, please lend me your power.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:56.090
I've received your help before, so tell me...

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.910
There's no mistaking it.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.090
This is the metal we need.

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:01.130
Yay!

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:02.900
Good job, Linca!

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:04.620
I'm happy that I could help!

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:05.890
Great job!

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:09.400
I'll refine it from here, and make the ingredients to reinforce the airship.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.480
Don't forget my contribution.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:13.640
Nice work.

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:14.400
Kept you waiting!

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:16.250
Wilbell-san!

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:18.080
Ta-da!

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:19.280
Amazing...

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.990
This is like a lump of solid fire.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.150
This is no big deal.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:25.190
If we use this to synthesize...

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:28.290
Please let me do it.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.820
Can you do it?

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:31.290
It's really difficult.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:33.210
Yes.

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.410
Don't worry.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:42.140
If I use everything that I learned up until now...!

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:05.790
Here.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:06.790
I'm counting on you.

00:19:34.180 --> 00:19:35.650
How is it?

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:37.280
It's done!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.250
We did it!

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.450
You really are amazing.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.410
It's your turn now, Logy-san.

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:49.240
Yeah.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.600
All right!

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.810
Yay! You did it!

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:03.780
Thanks, Escha.

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:08.630
There's no way we could have finished this without you and Logy.

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:12.250
Both your dream and Logy-san's dream have come true.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.690
That's right.

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:15.710
And now it's your turn.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:21.920
You completed it.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:23.760
Micie...

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.400
It's great that it went without a hitch.

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:26.340
I'm sorry.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:30.600
By the way, Logy-san, we received a letter for you.

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:32.640
Letter?

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:38.520
To my friend, Logy.

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:42.030
Don't give up on your dream!

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:59.180
We're finally leaving for the Unexplored Ruins!
